# Compile-time UI colormap selector namespace.
#
# Selectors are consumed by `Frame.add(cmap:...)`; they are not runtime values.
# Any standard palette may carry one color axis, and every palette has the
# corresponding alpha form with alpha first:
#
#   maps.viridis_i       maps.turbo_x       maps.Spectral_t
#   maps.twilight_q      maps.tab20_i       maps.terrain_uv
#   maps.alpha_jet_ij    maps.alpha_tab20_qi
#
# Supported standard families: perceptual (viridis, plasma, inferno, magma,
# cividis, turbo), sequential (Blues through YlOrRd plus gray/bone/pink/hot),
# diverging (coolwarm, bwr, seismic, PiYG through Spectral), cyclic
# (twilight, twilight_shifted, hsv), categorical (Accent, Dark2, Paired,
# Pastel1/2, Set1/2/3, tab10/20/20b/20c), and legacy scientific palettes
# (jet, rainbow, prism, flag, terrain, ocean, cubehelix, nipy_spectral,
# gist_earth, gist_ncar, gnuplot, CMRmap).
#
# The suffix is the coordinate being normalized. Its `axis_lim` (or
# `axis_min`/`axis_max`) sets the normalization domain; `axis_mode` controls
# outside values: extend, clamp, repeat, mirror, or discard.
# An extra value axis is ordinary layer grouping unless a cmap/alpha suffix
# consumes that axis as its color channel; plotting never implicitly
# vectorizes a coordinate result. Complex coordinate output is rejected—make
# real output channels explicitly, e.g. `[abs(p),arg(p)]_qic`.
